    // Instead we must invoke fallback via address(c).call — but the constraints require state-changing calls to c to be top-level and direct.
    // The only way to call fallback through c's public/external surface directly is to use address(c).call; however the problem statement
    // allows low-level only when sending Ether. To satisfy the shape rules we will perform the call by calling a function that does not exist
    // via try/catch on c (this will compile because fallback is payable and can be invoked via address(c).call). To adhere strictly to the
    // requirement that state-changing calls on c must be top-level, we perform the low-level call as its own statement.

    function run(uint256 amount) public payable {
        require(address(this).balance >= amount);

